#N canvas 20 20 1900 1200 12;
#X text 20 20 e_rush -- knob 4's far end \, in c_kit (Brendan \, 2026-11-05): "that recording keeps getting higher and higher pitched as the knob continues turning." The kit's whole output \, dry and wet \, is recorded all the time. Past the handoff the recording freezes \, the last steps of it loop at the rate asked \, up to 22 kHz \, and the live kit is muted \, ringing on underneath. c_steps says when. ref/module/sequencer.md, f 70;
#X text 20 190 creation args: none. signal inlet: the kit. inlet: on <span> <hz> \, span ms of recording played hz times a second \; rate <hz> <ms> \, the rate moved over ms \; and off \, it is let go. outlet~: the kit or its loop., f 70;
#X obj 20 340 inlet~;
#X obj 900 340 inlet;
#X obj 900 380 route on rate off;
#X obj 20 500 *~;
#X obj 200 460 line~;
#X obj 20 700 outlet~;
#X obj 20 400 e_rec \$0 3200;
#N canvas 200 200 1300 800 play 0;
#X text 20 20 The player \, on only while the loop plays. One head and no seam: the wrap's jump is part of the waveform \, as a retrigger's is \, and Brendan wants it raw all the way up \, nothing against aliasing. The rate goes on at the last message's ramp \, 20 ms \, so the knob's places do not zipper. The head goes where the phase says \, less 63 - i for a block's sample i \, as in e_tape (~/Sites/!reference/pure-data.md)., f 70;
