#X text 20 780 At the capture: the recorder fades out over three blocks and is stopped. Its head is then 192 samples past the step's boundary \, and the player starts as if it had started on the boundary. The loop ends 192 samples back from the head \, and 64 more are asked for: a delread4~ with no signal in sorts before its delwrite~ and reads a block nearer than asked \, and a block's worth of a 15 ms loop would be in the recorder's fade. Then the kit and the loop cross in 5 ms. The line holds 3.2 s \, c_steps keeping a span to 3 s \, 0.56 MB., f 50;
#X text 1000 1000 Let go: the kit and the loop cross back in 5 ms. Only once the player is silent does it stop and the recorder run on from where it stopped \, fading in. off during on's 5 ms \, or on during off's 6.7 ms \, cancels the other's delay \, and each path sets all it needs \, as in e_tape., f 50;
